# Milestone versioning

This rule is the single source for how milestones get their version and how milestone work is titled. `AGENTS.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md` and the other rules point here.

## The milestone's version

- A milestone's version is the `vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH` at the start of its GitHub milestone title. An optional short suffix may follow, for example `v1.3.0 Beta: Public UX & compliance`.
- Read it from the title, never from the milestone number:
  ```bash
  gh api 'repos/{owner}/{repo}/milestones?state=open&per_page=100' --jq '.[] | {number,title}'
  ```
  The `number` is only GitHub's internal ID. It must never appear in anything you name.

## The next milestone

1. Find the latest released tag: the highest `vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH` tag, for example from `git tag --list 'v*' --sort=-v:refname` or `gh release list`.
2. Take the open milestones whose title version is above that tag.
3. The next milestone is the one with the lowest version. Compare as semver, number by number (`0.58.3` < `0.59.0` < `0.100.0`), never as text and never by milestone number.

Stop and report to the owner, without guessing, if:

- a milestone title doesn't start with a valid `vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`, or
- the milestone's version is not above the latest released tag, or the version is already taken on `main`.

Don't rename, create or delete milestones yourself. Renaming one is the owner's decision.

## Names built from the version

Using the milestone `v1.3.0 Beta: Public UX & compliance`:

| Item | Format | Example |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Milestone branch | `milestone/v<MAJOR>-<MINOR>-<PATCH>[-<suffix-slug>]` | `milestone/v1-3-0-beta-public-ux` |
| Milestone PR into `main` | `v<version>: <suffix after the colon, or a summary>` | `v1.3.0: Public UX & compliance` |
| Issue PR into the milestone branch | `[v<version>] <issue title> (#<issue>)` | `[v1.3.0] Branded error pages (#123)` |
| Release history | `changelog/releases/v<version>.json` with `"version": "v<version>"` | `changelog/releases/v1.3.0.json` |
| Tag | `v<version>` | `v1.3.0` |
| GitHub Release title | `v<version>` (`release.yml` titles the Release with the tag) | `v1.3.0` |

- The suffix slug is short, lowercase kebab-case, taken from the title suffix.
- `release.yml` publishes the GitHub Release from the `v<version>` tag. Don't create it by hand.

## Version fields

- There are no version files to edit: the tag is the version. User-facing PRs add or update `changelog/releases/v<version>.json` for their milestone's version, or carry the `skip-changelog` label (see `docs/change-log-hub.md`).

## Never

Never write "Milestone 7", "#7" or "/milestone/7" (GitHub's milestone number) in a title, branch, commit subject, tag or release name.
